---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { business, addressLine, credentials, allCommunities } from '../data/site';
import { url, orgId } from '../lib/paths';

const title = 'About Us | OPP Approved Towing in Orillia | Lakeside';
const description =
  'Lakeside Towing & Recovery is a local, OPP approved towing company on Norweld Dr in Orillia. MTO Storage Certificate VS-212-186-623, licensed and insured.';

const trail = [{ name: 'About', href: '/about/' }];

const aboutSchema = {
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: title,
  description,
  mainEntity: { '@id': orgId(Astro.site!) },
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} breadcrumbs={trail} schema={[aboutSchema]}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About us"
    title="Your trusted towing partner"
    lede={`Lakeside Towing & Recovery is a local, full-service towing company based in Orillia. Emergency towing, winch-out and recovery work, roadside assistance and MTO-licensed storage — across Orillia and the surrounding area, with a truck on the road at any hour.`}
    trail={trail}
    facts={['OPP approved', 'MTO licensed', 'Based in Orillia', 'Open 24/7']}
  />

  <!-- ========================================================== Story -- -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap story">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>&ldquo;We Meet by Accident!&rdquo;</h2>
        <p>
          It is written on the side of the truck, and it is the honest summary of
          this business. Nobody plans to meet a tow operator. By the time you are
          reading our number, something has already gone wrong — the car will not
          start, the tank ran dry, the keys are visible on the driver&rsquo;s seat
          through a locked window, or there has been a collision.
        </p>
        <p>
          What we can control is what happens next. That means a person answering
          the phone rather than a queue, a realistic arrival time rather than an
          optimistic one, and a price agreed before a truck is dispatched rather
          than presented once your vehicle is already on the deck.
        </p>

        <h2>Local, and that matters</h2>
        <p>
          Our yard is at {addressLine}. Not a mailbox, not a call-forwarding
          number — the trucks and the storage are both here. A great many towing
          numbers that surface in a search are dispatch brokers who sell your call
          to whichever operator bids for it, which is how people end up waiting
          two hours for a truck coming from somewhere else entirely.
        </p>
        <p>
          Being based here also means we know the roads. Which stretches of
          Highway 11 hold snow when the forecast says the roads are fine. Which
          concession shoulders go soft in the spring thaw. Which cottage lanes off
          Rama Road stop being plowed in December. That knowledge is the
          difference between finding you quickly and driving past your turn twice.
        </p>

        <h2>What we actually do</h2>
        <p>
          24/7 emergency towing, winch-out and recovery, battery boosts,
          lockouts, fuel delivery, and secure indoor and outdoor vehicle
          storage. We serve Orillia and {allCommunities.length - 1} other
          communities across Simcoe County and south Muskoka.
        </p>
        <p>
          What we do not do is just as worth saying. We are not a long distance
          carrier — we do not run hauls to Toronto, Ottawa or Sudbury — and we do
          not operate an enclosed trailer for classics and exotics. We work our
          own patch. Orillia is in town; every other community we serve is
          treated as out of town and priced that way. If a job falls outside
          that, you will hear it from us on the first call rather than after a
          long wait.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are approved for Ontario Provincial Police calls, which means we work
          collision scenes regularly and understand how they are managed. Worth
          knowing: in Ontario, even when an officer arranges a tow at a scene, you
          are entitled to choose your own tow operator and where your vehicle is
          taken.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="story-aside">
        <div class="quote-card">
          <p class="quote">&ldquo;{business.tagline}&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="quote-attr">— on the side of every truck</p>
        </div>

        <div class="fact-card">
          <h2>At a glance</h2>
          <dl>
            <dt>Based in</dt>
            <dd>Orillia, Ontario</dd>
            <dt>Address</dt>
            <dd>{addressLine}</dd>
            <dt>Hours</dt>
            <dd>24 hours, 7 days, 365 days</dd>
            <dt>Phone</dt>
            <dd><a href={business.phoneHref}>{business.phoneDisplay}</a></dd>
            <dt>Email</dt>
            <dd><a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a></dd>
            <dt>Storage certificate</dt>
            <dd>MTO {business.storageCertificate}</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================================================== Credentials -- -->
  <section class="section section-navy">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Verified &amp; approved</p>
        <h2>Credentials</h2>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <p class="lede" style="margin-inline:auto">
          Towing is a licensed trade in Ontario for good reason. Here is exactly
          what we hold.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="cred-grid grid grid-4">
        {
          credentials.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <Icon name="badge-check" size={26} />
              <h3>{c.label}</h3>
              <p>{c.detail}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =================================================== Certificate -- -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cert">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
        <h2>MTO Vehicle Storage Certificate</h2>
        <hr class="rule" />
        <p>
          Certificate <strong>{business.storageCertificate}</strong>, issued by the
          Ontario Ministry of Transportation. It is what allows us to legally
          store vehicles, and it comes with obligations: proper records of what
          came in, when and in what condition, and specific rules about notifying
          owners and lienholders.
        </p>
        <p>
          That paper trail is not bureaucracy for its own sake. When an insurer
          starts asking questions about a total loss, or an adjuster needs to
          establish when a vehicle arrived and in what state, the documented
          record is the difference between a clean claim and a slow one. An
          unlicensed lot keeping an eye on things has none of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href={url('/services/vehicle-storage/')}>More about our storage service →</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="cert-figure">
        <img
          src={url('/media/mto-vehicle-storage-certificate.webp')}
          alt={`Ontario Ministry of Transportation Vehicle Storage Certificate ${business.storageCertificate} issued to Lakeside Towing & Recovery`}
          width="1100"
          height="1414"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>
          Ontario Ministry of Transportation Vehicle Storage Certificate
          {business.storageCertificate}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ====================================================== Standards -- -->
  <section class="section section-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="center">
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2>Four things we hold to</h2>
        <hr class="rule" />
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2 standards">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>The quoted price is the price</h3>
          <p>
            You hear a number on the phone before a truck is dispatched, and that
            is the number on the invoice. If something on scene genuinely changes
            the job, we tell you before we start — not after your vehicle is
            already loaded.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Honest arrival times</h3>
          <p>
            It is easy to say twenty minutes and turn up in ninety. We would
            rather tell you it will be an hour and be right. On a snowstorm night
            that honesty is worth more than optimism.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>No surcharge for the hour</h3>
          <p>
            A boost at 3 a.m. on a holiday costs the same as a boost at noon on a
            Tuesday. Charging a premium for the hours when people are most stuck
            is not how we want to run this.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>We say when we are not the answer</h3>
          <p>
            If a job needs a locksmith, a heavy-duty operator or a shop rather
            than a tow, we will tell you that on the phone. Sending a truck to a
            job we cannot finish helps nobody.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Layout>

<style>
  .story {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .story {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(270px, 0.8fr);
      gap: 3.25rem;
    }

    .story-aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: calc(var(--header-h) + 20px);
    }
  }

  .story-aside {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .quote-card {
    padding: 1.6rem;
    background: linear-gradient(150deg, var(--red), var(--red-deep));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .quote {
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .quote-attr {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 95%);
  }

  .fact-card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .fact-card h2 {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--navy-deep);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .fact-card dl {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .fact-card dt {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .fact-card dd {
    margin: 0.1rem 0 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .fact-card dd:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .cred-grid {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .cred-grid li {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 6%);
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 12%);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .cred-grid :global(.icon) {
    color: var(--sky);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .cred-grid h3 {
    font-size: 1.24rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .cred-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 72%);
  }

  .cert {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .cert {
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
      gap: 3.25rem;
    }
  }

  .cert p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .cert-figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cert-figure img {
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }

  .cert-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .standards {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .standards h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--navy-deep);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .standards p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
